      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: \nToday nights, I was able to play without a VPN.\nHe sat for 15 minutes and the server stopped responding.\nI spoke with people and move, but the social tab has stopped updating, and upload pictures of worlds, the Join button was also inactive.\nAlso, I could not select people with a laser to hide the avatar, when pressed, the menu with hide buttons did not appear.\nAfter updating the game to the new Unity, the exact same situation happened. (on the night of April 1 to 2)\nAfter that, I waited 2 days for the situation to improve, and on the 3rd day I set up a VPN.\nI have a static white ip and use Oculus CV1 and kinect360.\nVia VPN, this problem does not occur.\nI know other users with the same problem, but they do not want to write somewhere and just use the VPN.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-04-01T20:08:02.189Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "----------\nUPDATE: Posting my workaround from a below comment (YMMV):\nThe fix seemed to be disabling my 2.5gbit ethernet adapter, and instead using my 1gbit ethernet OR my WiFi OR a VPN (either of those 3 worked).\n----------\n\nRunning into this connection error, been having this issue since the open beta first started (Worked on previous version): https://i.imgur.com/MjSn4U6.png\nChecked the logs and I'm seeing this, it may be related (I can access this route via browser however, and VRChat.exe is allowed in my firewall):\n2020.04.01 14:56:47 Log        -  [API] [0] Sending Get request to https://api.vrchat.cloud/api/1/config?organization=vrchat\n2020.04.01 14:56:47 Log        -  [API] The response was null.\n2020.04.01 14:56:47 Error      -  [Always] Could not fetch fresh config file. Using cached if available.",
